A list region (`widget: 'object_list'`) must name its `idField`, the field its items' ids are kept in. Inka no longer assumes `@id` anywhere: a list region with no `idField` throws, naming the block and field. Before, a list keyed by another field (`key`, `field_id`) whose schema left it out was read as having no ids, and a reorder could empty it. A list keyed by `@id` now says so: `idField: '@id'`.
